W5 lazy tool disclosure (Dove fork). git apply ignores this preamble.

DOVE_TOOL_DISCLOSURE=lazy (also CUA_DRIVER_TOOL_DISCLOSURE, which
DOVE_DRIVER_TOOL_DISCLOSURE aliases to) shrinks the MCP tools/list. These
tools keep their full input schema: list_windows, get_window_state, run_steps,
verify_state, act (if registered) and describe_tools. Every other tool is
listed with a one-line description and {"type":"object"}. describe_tools
{names} returns the full entries. Withheld tools still run, and in lazy mode a
bad-arguments error carries the tool's input schema. Unset, behaviour is
upstream's. Applied on the core dispatcher (direct stdio and the daemon's HTTP
transport) and on the mcp proxy, which reads its own environment.

Size (user decision 2026-10-20, option A): the eager list is 225,763 bytes for
63 tools (0.37.0, Windows). The lazy limit is the measured size plus a small
margin (LAZY_TOOLS_LIST_LIMIT_BYTES in tool_disclosure_test.rs), about 20 KB,
not the 3 KB first planned. Every tool stays listed so clients such as Claude
Code, which only call listed tools, can call all 63. Bare name-only entries for
the 59 withheld tools already take 3.4 KB.

